Third-party code incorporated into SAPMAP
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Several SAPMAP modules port or adapt protocol logic from the pysap
project (https://github.com/OWASP/pysap, OWASP CBAS project, by
Martin Gallo / SecureAuth). pysap is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 2 or (at pysap's option) any later version —
GPLv2-or-later. Because SAPMAP incorporates pysap-derived code, the
combined work is licensed under the GPL as well; this is why SAPMAP
as a whole is distributed under GPLv3 rather than a permissive
license such as Apache-2.0 (Apache-2.0 code cannot be combined with
GPLv2-only code, but GPLv2-or-later code — like pysap's — is
compatible with GPLv3).

Files with pysap-derived logic include (non-exhaustive):
  * modules/protocols/sap_rsec_cipher.py
  * modules/protocols/sap_snc.py
  * modules/protocols/sap_router_info.py
  * modules/protocols/sap_saprouter.py
  * modules/exploitation/sap_gw_xpg_standalone.py
  * modules/exploitation/sap_ms_betrusted.py
  * modules/discovery/sap_client_enum.py
  * modules/discovery/sapmap_scanner.py
  * modules/discovery/sapmap_rfc.py
  * modules/data_extraction/sapmap_secstore.py
  * modules/data_extraction/sapmap_scc_ssfs_decrypt.py
  * modules/postex/sap_pse_loot.py

  * tools/sap_decompress/sap_decompress
      Precompiled ELF binary that decompresses SAP's proprietary
      LZH format (used inside GET_TABLEBLOCK_COMPRESSED_RFC
      responses).  Built from pysap's pysapcompress module.  See
      tools/sap_decompress/README.md for provenance and rebuild
      instructions.

